.TH AURA-BROWSER 7 "2026-04-18" "Aura 0.1.0" "Aura Manual"
.SH NAME
aura\-browser \- browser automation tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
Control a headless browser from aura. Backed by the
.B agent-browser
CLI.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The browser tool enables the LLM to drive a real Chromium instance for
authenticated, JS-rendered, or form-based sites. Sessions persist cookies
and local storage across tool calls within the same Discord thread.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B run
Run a bounded Jev task on the current page. Requires
.BR goal .
This optional action appears only when
.B AURA_BROWSER_JEV_ENABLED=true
is set. Use navigate first if needed. The action reuses the selected session,
including an optional CDP connection. It does not create or close tabs.
The timeout argument applies to the whole run (default 90 seconds, maximum 600).
The run stops after 30 actions or 60 decisions. Stale decisions count toward
the decision limit. Field text requests also count in the reported model_calls.
.PP
A done_unverified result is a model decision. Verify the final observation
before reporting task completion. A blocked or auth_required result returns
control to Aura. An uncertain result means an input command can have taken
effect. Inspect the page before continuing; do not repeat the entire task.
The run supports common HTML controls, text replacement, native dropdowns,
page scrolling, and waits. Use existing actions for uploads and other
unsupported workflows. Frames, shadow roots, pop-up tabs, canvas, nested
scrolling, and arbitrary keyboard controls are outside this loop.
.TP
.B navigate
Open a URL. Returns a compact snapshot of the page automatically.
.TP
.B snapshot
Return the current page's accessibility tree with element refs
.RB ( @e1 ,
.BR @e2 ,
...). Pass
.B full=true
for the complete tree.
.TP
.B click
Click the element identified by
.BR ref .
.TP
.B type
Type
.B text
into the input identified by
.BR ref .
.TP
.B press
Press a key
.RB ( Enter ,
.BR Tab ,
.BR Escape ,
.BR ArrowDown ,
...).
.TP
.B back
Navigate back in history.
.TP
.B vision
Screenshot the page and ask the vision model about it. Useful for
captcha, visual layout, or things the accessibility tree misses.
.SH SESSIONS
Sessions are auto-scoped per Discord thread via
.BR channel_id .
Two threads get two isolated browsers. Use the
.B session
argument for a named session shared across threads or for scheduled
tasks with no thread context.
.SH CDP ATTACH
Pass
.B cdp_url
to attach to a user-controlled Chromium with
.B --remote-debugging-port
enabled. Useful when auth is maintained in openclaw or the user's own
Chrome profile.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Aura does not log in automatically. For authenticated sites:
.IP \(bu 2
Start
.B agent-browser
interactively on Eisenhower, log in manually. The session persists.
.IP \(bu 2
OR start a browser with remote debugging enabled and pass
.B cdp_url
to aura.
.PP
If a navigation lands on a login page, the tool returns
.B AUTH_REQUIRED
and stops. The LLM surfaces this to you.
.SH SAFETY
Two tool-layer blocks, no user override in v1:
.IP \(bu 2
URLs targeting private/internal IPs or localhost are blocked (SSRF).
.IP \(bu 2
URLs containing API keys / tokens in query parameters are blocked
(exfiltration via prompt injection).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/aura-browser-<session>/
Per-session socket directory for the agent-browser daemon.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AURA_BROWSER_JEV_ENABLED
Set exactly true to expose the optional run action. Default: disabled.
Set this and the provider variables in Aura's process environment, then restart
Aura to refresh the tool instructions.
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_API_KEY
Set this in ~/.config/aura/.env on the deployment host. Aura reads the file
at startup. Keep its permissions at 0600 and restart Aura after a change.
Required for run. Used only by the TypeSafe choice client.
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_MODEL
TypeSafe model name. Default: jev-latest.
.TP
.B TEXT_MODEL_API_KEY
Credential for the field text provider. Required for Chat Completions models.
Not used when TEXT_MODEL starts with openai-codex/.
.TP
.B TEXT_MODEL_BASE_URL
HTTPS API base URL for an OpenAI-compatible text provider.
Aura appends /chat/completions.
Required for Chat Completions models. Not used for openai-codex/ models.
.TP
.B TEXT_MODEL
Required for run. Model name accepted by the text provider.
Use openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna for GPT text entry through Aura's existing Codex
login. This route uses low reasoning and the existing Responses stream parser.
The request stops when its deadline expires or the browser worker terminates.
.PP
The run sends page text, visible field values, the goal, and recent action
context to TypeSafe. It sends field context to the text provider when text is
needed. Credentials are not tool arguments. Diagnostic output contains counts
and timing; the final observation is returned to Aura as tool output.
.TP
.B AURA_BROWSER_CDP_URL
Optional default CDP endpoint. Can still be overridden per tool call.
.TP
.B AURA_BROWSER_TIMEOUT_MS
Override default per-action timeout (default 30000).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aura (1),
.BR aura\-flares (7),
.BR aura\-config (5),
.BR aura\-diagnostics (7),
.BR agent-browser (1).
